  "findings": [
    "Both arms passed every required customer, financial, queue, diagnostic and restoration gate; 18000 scheduled/dispatched/confirmed and unique paid-issued tickets each, zero errors/drops and no observed duplicate bookings.",
    "Control callback HTTP deltas were primary-only. Candidate successful callback requests were observed on every API, with approximately half reaching secondary APIs. These are bracketing request counters, not counts of distinct payments.",
    "One-factor matched comparison measured lower end-to-end and payment-to-ticket p95 and lower primary CPU. Status polling changed only modestly; no polling configuration was changed.",
    "Both arms used frozen binaries and gateway delays. Local bank-like simulator changes and the published SWR candidate were deliberately excluded.",
    "This is one 60 journeys/s five-minute pair. It does not establish 84 successful tickets/s, maximum production RPS, or 300000 tickets/hour."
  ],
  "next_action": "Compare fixed shared callback routing with 2+2 versus 1+3 API placement, keeping workload and aggregate budgets unchanged; create and locally qualify the exact registered profile first. Then attempt 84 tickets/s if the measured gates pass."
